      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Secrets Management**\n\nI'm currently focused on how to securely retrieve the API key using Python. I've decided to use AWS Secrets Manager as the external secrets store. My next step will be to concretely integrate AWS Secrets Manager into the `fetch_api_key.py` script.\n\n\n**Implementing the Script**\n\nI've outlined a basic plan for creating `fetch_api_key.py`. I'm going to start by creating the file and writing Python code. I'll use `boto3` to retrieve a secret from AWS Secrets Manager. To do this I will need to specify the region and secret name, which I will use placeholders for, assuming env variables will be used in the future.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789818142819,
          "start": 1789818139878
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b97974e6001CM4nV2CLJS9n9R",
      "message_id": "msg_0b9796fa3001w8EuCbNvY91Lmz",
      "session_id": "ses_f468690dbffedYkC98gmdhzBat",
      "time_created": 1789818139878,
      "time_updated": 1789818142819
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "LMGSr20pcMxBPEYz",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\nimport os\n\ndef fetch_api_key(secret_name: str, region_name: str = \"us-east-1\") -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Fetches an API key from AWS Secrets Manager.\n\n    Args:\n        secret_name: The name of the secret to retrieve.\n        region_name: The AWS region where the secret is stored.\n                     Defaults to \"us-east-1\".\n\n    Returns:\n        The retrieved API key.\n\n    Raises:\n        Exception: If the secret cannot be retrieved.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create a Secrets Manager client\n    client = boto3.client(\"secretsmanager\", region_name=region_name)\n\n    try:\n        get_secret_value_response = client.get_secret_value(SecretId=secret_name)\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise Exception(f\"Failed to retrieve secret '{secret_name}': {e}\")\n\n    # Decrypts secret using the associated KMS key.\n    # Depending on whether the secret is a string or binary, one of these fields will be populated.\n    if \"SecretString\" in get_secret_value_response:\n        return get_secret_value_response[\"SecretString\"]\n    else:\n        # For binary secrets, you would typically decode them here.\n        # For this task, we assume the API key is a string.\n        raise Exception(\"Secret is not a string type.\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Example usage:\n    # Set environment variables AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, and AWS_REGION\n    # or configure AWS CLI with 'aws configure'\n    \n    # Replace with your actual secret name\n    api_secret_name = os.environ.get(\"API_SECRET_NAME\", \"your/secret/name\") \n    aws_region = os.environ.get(\"AWS_REGION\", \"us-east-1\")\n\n    try:\n        api_key = fetch_api_key(api_secret_name, aws_region)\n        print(f\"Successfully fetched API key (first 5 chars): {api_key[:5]}...\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n",
            "filePath": "fetch_api_key.py"
          },
